+# Changelog
+
+All notable Modary changes are recorded here. The format follows semantic
+versioning terminology, while every pre-v1 release remains an Alpha contract
+unless its release notes explicitly state otherwise.
+
+## v0.1.0-alpha.1 - Unreleased
+
+### Added
+
+- Release-readiness documentation, policies, and validation design for the
+  first remotely consumable Alpha.
+
+### Release blockers
+
+- The owner must select a redistribution license.
+- The canonical remote repository must be configured and its visibility chosen.
+- `v0.1.0-alpha.1` must be created only from the final validated candidate.
+- Remote Go module consumption must pass after the tag is available.
+
+## F0 Technical Acceptance - 2026-07-31
+
+### Added
+
+- Independent Go framework packages for Actions, modules, application assembly,
+  application commands, project tooling, HTTP/MCP transport, identity,
+  authorization, audit, database access, execution scope, and official adapters.
+- Deterministic module lifecycle, capability ownership, governed Preview and
+  Execute semantics, SQLite-backed transactions, idempotency, and audit.
+- Independent external-consumer conformance, generated contracts, cross-build,
+  race, repetition, fuzz, source-stability, and neutrality gates.
+
+This entry records technical acceptance, not a distributed version. There is no
+corresponding public tag or release until the release process is completed.
